Z||000000||engine18||02-15-2000||12:51 PM||||I'm upgrading my wheels to 17" and I need to know a good tire size... I have seen various tire sizes and I'm not able to determine what best for me... I have a 84 2m4 with no change in suspension...yet.  Thanks for any suggestions.....||||reg||5
Z||000001||1FST2M6||02-15-2000||01:27 PM||||I had 215-40-17s on the front and 235-40s on the rear.. I started out with 245s but a door in the road killed those.. Yokohama A520s were very sticky and had decent rain stability. Yours are a 17x7 right? Dunlop w10s are a decent tire too.. but they don't last very long, a set of eibachs would make it look that much sharper..  Have 18s now.. just waiting for tire money... What wheels do you have?  a pic of my car... <A HREF="http://www.freeyellow.com/members/fiero/travis.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.freeyellow.com/members/fiero/travis.html</A> ||||reg||1
Z||000002||88 Fiero||02-15-2000||02:16 PM||||I got 255/35/17 in the rear and 225/40/17 in the fronts.....||||reg||1
Z||000003||Spyder||02-15-2000||02:53 PM||||This is what I have on the front:<BR>215/40WR17 Yokohama A520 on a 17x7.5 rim<BR>When it is time to change tires I’ll replace them with like a 225 instead of the 215.<BR>Here is the comparison picture of the 17s and the stock.<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.mindspring.com/~mm889-19/wheelcompa.jpg">  <p>[This message has been edited by Spyder (edited 02-15-2000).]||||reg||1
